  "verbalization": "Orotinin is shown to have a target of HaCaT cells in all three provided paths, suggesting a potential interaction between the compound and skin-derived cells. The HaCaT cells are identified as targets of multiple flavonoid-like compounds, including 5,7,3',4',5'-Pentahydroxy-3,6,8-trimethoxyflavone and (1R,4R)-4-Hydroxydauca-7-Ene-6,9-Dione, which in turn target the CD276 antigen. This indicates that Orotinin may act through a pathway involving flavonoid-like molecules that modulate CD276 expression or function in HaCaT cells. The presence of multiple distinct molecular entities that share the same target suggests a potential mechanism of action involving the regulation of CD276, possibly through the activation or inhibition of signaling pathways that are influenced by these compounds. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Orotinin and CD276, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
